<!-- Usage Rules - Do's and Don'ts -->
<div class="page page-content">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="accent-bar"></div>
    <h1>Usage Rules & Guidelines</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Protecting your brand integrity</p>
  </div>
  
  <div class="section-body">
    <p>{{usageRulesText}}</p>
    
    <div class="dos-donts-grid">
      <div class="dd-card do">
        <div class="dd-title">DO</div>
        <ul class="dd-list">
          <li>Use approved brand colors</li>
          <li>Maintain minimum clear space around logo</li>
          <li>Use on solid, contrasting backgrounds</li>
          <li>Scale proportionally</li>
          <li>Use high-resolution files for print</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      
      <div class="dd-card dont">
        <div class="dd-title">DON'T</div>
        <ul class="dd-list">
          <li>Stretch or distort the logo</li>
          <li>Change logo colors arbitrarily</li>
          <li>Place on busy or low-contrast backgrounds</li>
          <li>Rotate or tilt the logo</li>
          <li>Add effects like shadows or outlines</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    <h2>Clear Space Requirements</h2>
    <p>Always maintain a minimum clear space around the logo equal to the height of the letter "x" in the logotype. This ensures the logo remains visible and uncluttered.</p>
    
    <h2>Minimum Size</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Print:</strong> Minimum 25mm wide</li>
      <li><strong>Digital:</strong> Minimum 80px wide</li>
      <li><strong>Favicon:</strong> 16px × 16px (simplified version)</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h2>Color Variations</h2>
    <p>Use the appropriate logo version based on background:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Primary:</strong> Full color on white/light backgrounds</li>
      <li><strong>Reversed:</strong> White version on dark backgrounds</li>
      <li><strong>Single Color:</strong> Black or white for special applications</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  
  <div class="page-footer">
    <span>{{businessName}} Brand Guidelines</span>
    <span>{{pageNumber}}</span>
  </div>
</div>
